# harness/field/scenarios/klldap-swap.expect: where klldap-swap.sh's rust leg is known to differ from its MIT leg,
# by check name (the INFO observations of checks.tsv). The comparison of the two legs grades a listed check KNOWN;
# anything else that differs is a finding. Each line names the hand record that shows the difference (in the
# archive of field records) and the package that removes it, or the decision that keeps it.
# check	known difference (rust leg vs MIT)	record	owned by
obs.image.krb5	krb5-server is not installed: the swap itself (f-F3's one Dockerfile hunk); krb5-libs, krb5-workstation and libkadm5 stay the image's MIT 1.21.3	f-F3 README ("KLLDAP change"), build/Dockerfile.diff	decision: the swap (F3)
obs.boot.sockets	TCP 750 is listened on as well (KLLDAP's kdc.conf: kdc_ports = 750,88, no kdc_tcp_ports), as MIT 1.22.2 does; the image's MIT 1.21.3 listens on UDP 750 only	f-F3 README finding 3; f-F3 oracle/kdc-tcp-ports.txt	decision: MIT 1.22.2's behaviour, not a defect
obs.boot.json	the daemons' JSON log goes to stdout, so into docker logs (f-F3: 548 lines for a boot and 25 operations); MIT's daemons write none there	f-F3 README (the contract table's JSON row); docs/install.md "Logs"	decision: the F3 ruling (O0082), a note only
obs.boot.logs	kadmind.log is 0640, made by kadmind; MIT's is 0600, as kdb5_util create writes it first: our kdb5_util and kadmin.local do not log	f-F3 README finding 5 (known since P3)	open item "the tools' own log" (no package yet)
obs.boot.kdb	the dump-format store: principal is a dump file, beside principal.ulog, and there is no principal.kadm5 (MIT: the db2 principal and principal.kadm5)	f-F3 README finding 5 (known since P3); docs/install.md "Beside krb5-server"	decision: kerber-rust's store format (a realm moves over by dump and load)
obs.ffi.alma10.admin	the lane's sandbox makes admin/admin with addprinc -pw and its kdc.conf sets no default_principal_flags, so it gets REQUIRES_PRE_AUTH; MIT's Attributes line is empty	f-F3 README finding 4; f-F3 ffi/sandbox-diff-vs-f3-mit.txt	decision: preauth by default, docs/mit-deviations.md STRICTER row "kadm5 create default attributes"
obs.ffi.f43.admin	as obs.ffi.alma10.admin, beside Fedora 43's MIT 1.22.2 client	f-F3 ffi/sandbox-diff-vs-f3-mit.txt	as obs.ffi.alma10.admin
